: \"Update README.md\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Scaffold solution, projects (src + tests), csproj files","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement data models for matches, players","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement CSV loaders for all 6 files with name normalization","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement query services (match, team, player, competition, stats)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement MCP stdio JSON-RPC server with tools","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write BDD GWT xUnit tests","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build and run tests, fix issues","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update README.md","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}],"truncated":false},"title":"8 todos","time":{"start":1782087308577,"end":1782087308578}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The guide is identical to TASK.md. Now let me plan the implementation. I'll create:\n\n1. A C# solution with:\n   - `BrazilianSoccerMcp` - main MCP server library/console app with data loading, querying, stats\n   - `BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests` - BDD-style tests using xUnit / SpecFlow-like GWT structure\n\nI'll keep it simple - use stdio MCP server using the official MCP SDK for C# if available. But since tooling is \"none\", I'll implement an MCP-compatible stdio server manually using JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio. This is most reliable.\n\nLet me design:\n\n**Project structure:**\n- `BrazilianSoccerMcp.sln`\n- `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/BrazilianSoccerMcp.csproj` - console app (MCP server via stdio JSON-RPC)\n- `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Program.cs` - entry point\n- `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/` - data models & loaders\n- `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Services/` - query services\n- `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Mcp/` - MCP protocol server\n- `tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests.csproj` - xUnit BDD GWT tests\n\nLet me start building. I'll use CsvHelper for CSV parsing since it handles edge cases well. Actually let me just use the built-in `System.IO` + a simple parser since CsvHelper requires package. Actually CsvHelper is widely available via NuGet, so let's use it.\n\nLet me create a plan with TodoWrite.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecae551b001d1XSjbOoU65z96","sessionID":"ses_11352285affesfmj6vH5c5sk25","messageID":"msg_eecae2b08001xWkVgYxJOHJIeU"}}
