{"type":"text","timestamp":1782087823147,"sessionID":"ses_11352285affesfmj6vH5c5sk25","part":{"id":"prt_eecb61e0a001AtYXDdun2knIjQ","messageID":"msg_eecb60df0001kAST0O60mQgvw6","sessionID":"ses_11352285affesfmj6vH5c5sk25","type":"text","text":"Done. Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server in C#/.NET 10 as specified in TASK.md.\n\n**What was built:**\n- `BrazilianSoccerMcp.sln` with `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp` (server) and `tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests` (xUnit BDD tests)\n- CSV loaders (`DataRepository.cs`) for all 6 Kaggle files with team-name normalization (`TeamNameNormalizer.cs`) handling suffixes, accents, and parenthesised noise so cross-file joins work\n- Query services: `MatchService`, `TeamService`, `PlayerService`, `CompetitionService` (standings, biggest victories, averages)\n- Hand-rolled MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio (`McpServer.cs` + `ToolRegistry.cs`) exposing 10 tools (`search_matches`, `head_to_head`, `team_stats`, `search_teams`, `search_players`, `players_by_club`, `standings`, `biggest_victories`, `match_averages`, `seasons`)\n- 23 Given/When/Then tests covering matches, teams, players, competitions, and the MCP protocol itself\n\n**Verification:** `dotnet build` succeeds with 0 warnings/errors, `dotnet test` passes 23/23, and an end-to-end stdio smoke test (`initialize` → `tools/list` → `tools/call`) returns valid JSON-RPC responses (e.g. Flamengo vs Fluminense head-to-head: 31–25–21 across 77 matches).\n\nNote: had to add `Directory.Build.props` setting `GitRepositoryConfigurationScope=local` because the .NET 10 SDK's built-in `Microsoft.Build.Tasks.Git` was failing on sandboxed `~/.gitconfig` access. Also documented in the README that the bundled FIFA 19 snapshot has no Brazilian clubs (only European), so player-by-Brazilian-club queries use European clubs.","time":{"start":1782087818762,"end":1782087823144}}}
